# Actions that perform no authorization check.
#
# Authorization in KnowWE actions is opt-in: /action/* has no security-constraint, AbstractAction checks
# nothing, and the wiki connector does not either - storeAttachment, createArticle and
# writeArticleToWikiPersistence are plain persistence calls. Every action therefore has to decide about the
# access rights of the user itself.
#
# This list is the state we found, so that the enforcer rule requireAuthorizationCheck can keep it from
# growing. It may only get shorter: an action that is not on it and performs no check fails the build, and an
# action on it that performs a check by now fails as well, asking for its entry to be removed.
#
# When you take an entry off the list, please say in the commit what the action reads or writes, so the next
# reader can tell a real check from a formality. When you add one, put the reason behind it as a comment.
#
# Regenerate with: mvn -Ddenkbares.enforcer.report=true -DskipTests process-classes
